32:["$","p",null,{"children":["where the first segment is the scheduler's ",["$","code",null,{"children":"name"}]," from the config (the route\nparameter is called ",["$","code",null,{"children":"instance_name"}]," in the source, but it is looked up against\nscheduler names). Anyone who can issue that request can drain every worker in\nyour fleet, one ",["$","code",null,{"children":"worker_id"}]," at a time, and your builds stop. No credential protects it. It\nis also the endpoint you will legitimately want during an incident (see\n",["$","$L61",null,{"href":"/operate/runbooks#a-worker-is-oom-killed","children":"Runbooks"}],"), so the answer is to make\nit reachable from your operator network and nowhere else, not to disable it."]}]
