48:["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"use_native_roots: true"}]," trusts the host's system trust store instead of a\nnamed CA. Convenient against a public endpoint, wrong against an internal one:\nit means any publicly-trusted certificate for that hostname is accepted."]}]
49:["$","$L1b",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-sandbox-is-not-a-security-boundary","children":"The sandbox is not a security boundary"}]
4a:["$","p",null,{"children":["For isolation from state left by an earlier action, development builds offer\nthe opt-in ",["$","$L61",null,{"href":"/reference/forge-config/main#localworkerconfig","children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"single_use"}]," lifecycle"]}],".\nIt requires a launcher that replaces the container and its writable volumes\nafter every action. This prevents reuse of local files, background processes,\nand worker caches. It does not create a new kernel boundary or make untrusted\nactions safe on a privileged container host. Continue applying the network\nand process restrictions described on this page."]}]
4b:["$","p",null,{"children":["The development-only\n",["$","$L61",null,{"href":"/reference/forge-config/main#buck2filecaptureconfig","children":["$","code",null,{"children":"experimental_buck2_file_capture"}]}],"\noption additionally runs an operator-supplied collector inside that dedicated\nLinux container. Configure it to exclude platform credentials and internal\ncaches, and use narrowly scoped credentials for its ingest service. The hook\ndoes not isolate a token from action processes with the same user privileges.\nThe collector and\nits ingest service must enforce authorization and filesystem boundaries.\nInvocation metadata identifies the client request; it does not authenticate its\nowner. Separate action mount namespaces and entrypoint wrappers are rejected so\nthe collector cannot accidentally archive the outer worker's filesystem."]}]
4c:["$","p",null,{"children":["Workers can be configured with ",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_namespaces: true"}]," and\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_mount_namespace: true"}],". Both are real, and neither makes an action safe to\nrun on your behalf."]}]
4d:["$","p",null,{"children":"What the worker actually does before executing an action:"}]
4e:["$","$L62",null,{"className":"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","style":{"--shiki-light":"#24292e","--shiki-dark":"#e1e4e8","--shiki-light-bg":"#fff","--shiki-dark-bg":"#24292e"},"tabIndex":"0","icon":"<svg viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M 6,1 C 4.354992,1 3,2.354992 3,4 v 16 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 12 c 1.645008,0 3,-1.354992 3,-3 V 8 7 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 20.707031,6.2929687 l -5,-5 A 1.0001,1.0001 0 0 0 15,1 h -1 z m 0,2 h 7 v 3 c 0,1.645008 1.354992,3 3,3 h 3 v 11 c 0,0.564129 -0.435871,1 -1,1 H 6 C 5.4358712,21 5,20.564129 5,20 V 4 C 5,3.4358712 5.4358712,3 6,3 Z M 15,3.4140625 18.585937,7 H 16 C 15.435871,7 15,6.5641288 15,6 Z\" fill=\"currentColor\" /></svg>","children":["$","$L63",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"unshare(CLONE_NEWPID | CLONE_NEWUSER | CLONE_NEWIPC | CLONE_NEWUTS)"}]}],"\n",["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"write /proc/self/setgroups  \"deny\""}]}],"\n",["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"write /proc/self/uid_map    \"<uid> <uid> 1\""}]}],"\n",["$","span",null,{"className":"line","children":["$","span",null,{"children":"write /proc/self/gid_map    \"<gid> <gid> 1\""}]}]]}]}]}]
4f:["$","a",null,{"href":"https://github.com/toxicwind/forge/blob/v1.6.5/forge-worker/src/namespace_utils.rs","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","data-source-link":"forge-worker/src/namespace_utils.rs","data-source-ref":"v1.6.5","title":"forge-worker/src/namespace_utils.rs at v1.6.5","className":"inline-flex items-center gap-1 rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 align-middle font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground no-underline transition-colors hover:border-brand/50 hover:text-brand","children":[["$","svg",null,{"width":"12","height":"12","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","aria-hidden":"true","children":["$","path",null,{"d":"m16 18 6-6-6-6M8 6l-6 6 6 6"}]}],"unshare"]}]
50:["$","p",null,{"children":["Read the uid map carefully. It is an ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"identity"}]," map: uid ",["$","em",null,{"children":"N"}]," inside the\nnamespace is uid ",["$","em",null,{"children":"N"}]," outside it. The action runs as the worker's own user, with\nthe worker's own privileges on the host filesystem. This is not a\nuid-remapping sandbox; it is a process-reaping and hermeticity mechanism. PID\nnamespacing means orphaned children die with the action instead of leaking;\nIPC and UTS namespacing means actions cannot see each other's semaphores or\nhostname (the hostname is set to ",["$","code",null,{"children":"forge"}],"). With ",["$","code",null,{"children":"use_mount_namespace"}],"\nthe flag list also gains ",["$","code",null,{"children":"CLONE_NEWNS"}],", the worker's own root action\ndirectory is masked so one action cannot see another's tree, and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp"}]," is\nreplaced with the action's own temporary directory, on the worker's disk and\nremoved with the action, so actions cannot collide on, or leak state\nthrough, predictable paths there (",["$","code",null,{"children":"isolate_tmp: false"}]," keeps the host's\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp"}]," visible; the bound ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp"}]," carries the work volume's mount options,\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"noexec"}]," included, not the host ",["$","code",null,{"children":"/tmp"}],"'s); the rest of the host filesystem\nstays visible."]}]
51:["$","p",null,{"children":["Note what is absent from that flag list: ",["$","strong",null,{"children":["$","code",null,{"children":"CLONE_NEWNET"}]}],". No network\nnamespace is created. An action has the worker's full network access, including to port\n50061 on your scheduler, and to anything else on the worker's network."]}]
52:["$","p",null,{"children":"An action can, by design:"}]
53:["$","ul",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Read and write every file the worker's user can, outside its work directory"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Open a connection to the worker API and register as a worker"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":"Reach any internal service the worker host can reach"}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":["Consume the whole host's memory and CPU, since there is no per-action limit\nof any kind in the configuration; the only bound is\n",["$","$L61",null,{"href":"/operate/runbooks#a-worker-is-oom-killed","children":[["$","code",null,{"children":"max_inflight_tasks"}]," and the container's own limits"]}]]}],"\n"]}]
54:["$","p",null,{"children":["The practical stance: ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"treat the right to submit an action as equivalent to\nshell access on a worker host."}]," Then the controls follow: workers on their own\nnetwork segment with egress rules, no ambient cloud credentials on worker\ninstance profiles, no shared secrets in the worker's environment, and a worker\nhost you are willing to rebuild."]}]
55:["$","p",null,{"children":["Containerising the worker helps only as far as your container runtime is a\nboundary. The shipped Compose executor runs ",["$","code",null,{"children":"privileged: true"}]," precisely so\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"unshare"}]," works, which removes most of what the container was giving you."]}]
